          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap5/chapter5s31.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap5/chapter5s31.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "स्निग्धत्वं पल्लवेभ्यो मृगिनयनमनिन्द्रादितः सविलासं... एवं हि संविधाय नारीं विधात्रा सृष्टा ॥",
          "iast": "snigdhatvaṁ pallavebhyo mṛginayanamanindrāditaḥ savilāsam... evaṁ hi saṁvidhāya nārīṁ vidhātrā sṛṣṭā ||",
          "translation": "Taking the tenderness of the blossom, the glance of the doe, the gaiety of sunbeams, the inconstancy of the wind, and the fidelity of the dove—the Creator blended these together and fashioned Woman, the supreme adornment of the universe."
